  "title": "Francine M NDE 6656",
  "date": "17 Février 1973",
  "content": "I was under anesthesia during the birth of my second child. All of a sudden, I found myself hovering at ceiling level and viewing the scene under me but I really wasn't very much interested in what was happening down there! I remember mentally nudging myself to 'pay attention to what's going on' but then I found myself floating in a nebula of extreme beauty. I was immersed in the depths of the sky, or 'heaven' and I felt a 'presence' but did not try to see it. Immediately I understood the whole universe—and for me, understanding all those scientific things, (never having been good at math and science in school) it was like a rejuvenating fountain! Furthermore, I had gone through much suffering during my youth—and now I was able to understand why. And then, quite simply, I woke up in the post-operative recovery room. I was completely certain of everything and wanted to tell my doctor all about it as quickly as possible. Unfortunately, he advised me to forget it, if I did not want to wind up in the madhouse [mental hospital]. So after that, I kept it a secret. Right now I can't find words strong enough to explain how much this experience changed me, but I can state strongly that I have never had any doubts that I lived through every second of it.",
